56	Company Website	CORPORATE_WEBSITE	https://www.lemantrust.ch	Home	PRESERVE YOUR HERITAGEFOR THE NEXT GENERATION\nPRESERVEYOUR HERITAGEFOR THE NEXTGENERATION\nWe are a Swiss company incorporated in 1990, fully independent and owned by the founding family.\nLemantrust SA was created as a family office to provide the founding family with a professional and transparent vehicle to oversee, manage and grow their wealth on a long-term horizon.\nBut who better to understand the needs of a family than another family itself?\nSo the business model was extended to provide wealth management & family office services to a limited and selected number of families sharing the same concerns.\nToday, as a multifamily office, we do not only manage the wealth of our client families, we develop solutions that allow the protection of their assets, while never loosing focus of the objectives and projects of our client. We are by their side every step of the way.\nOur clients are more than clients….\nOUR MISSION	\N	fr	2022-07-05 00:00:00+00	2026-08-27 12:54:37.285767+00	{}
57	Company Website	CORPORATE_WEBSITE	https://www.msmiam.ch	MSM Investment Advisors SA	MSM believes passionately in its core values as a guide to serving our client’s interests.\nCommitment & Excellence\nOur board and senior leadership bring decades of experience from leading global financial institutions, complemented by our dedicated teams in Geneva and Dubai. Together, we combine commitment and excellence with more than a century of collective service to our global families.\nTransparency & Trust\nTrusted for decades, we bring seasoned expertise from leading global financial institutions. With transparency at our core, we guide clients through complex multi‑jurisdictional tax and regulatory challenges with clarity and confidence.\nIntegrity & Agreement\nWe partner with families to evaluate investment strategies, helping them identify those that create value and align with their goals, ultimately leading to successful outcomes. Our compensation is based solely on the value we deliver to the families we serve.\nGlobal network of strategic partners and alliances\nExpert guidance across borders, built on trust, clarity, and results. MSM is a multi-family office dedicated to providing wealth management services to global families.\n“Our families’ collective net worth are in excess of USD 5 billion and their wealth is spread across three continents. Generational wealth from first-generation entrepreneurs is a powerful force, but its global, multi-continental spread demands bespoke, privacy-first wealth management that is as agile and ambitious as its creators.”\nMilan S. Morjaria is the Founder of MSM Investment Advisors SA, with over 38 years of experience in global financial markets. Drawing on his extensive background, he founded MSM Multi Family Office in Geneva in March 2010, later expanding its operations to Dubai in August 2020. The firm specializes in managing the wealth, transitions, and legacies of affluent global families and their charitable foundations.\nFrom 1988 to 2010, Milan built a distinguished 22-year career at Citigroup. He progressed through diverse roles, from currency trader and private banker to his final position as a Managing Director in Geneva, where he focused on Ultra High Net Worth clients and family offices. During his tenure, he was a member of the European leadership team and was a three-time recipient of the prestigious Chairman’s Council European Award (2005-2007). He also served on the board and investment committee for the Citibank Swiss pension fund.\nMilan holds a bachelor’s degree in economics from the London School of Economics and Political Sciences and has completed executive programs at London Business School and Harvard Business School.\nA resident of Switzerland, he is deeply committed to philanthropy, supporting Swiss non-profit organizations focused on children’s education and healthcare in developing countries.\nHe travels extensively to the United Kingdom, the Middle East, and India, where he maintains both family and business interests.\nRodney Allen\nChairman and Board Member\n“Families face ever-increasing complexities: businesses and investments expand into new countries, sons and daughters take up lives abroad, assets grow beyond any imaginable needs to name a few. These families look for help in managing this complexity, but traditional financial-services providers often fall short. At MSM we sit on the family’s side of the table. With its customized Family Office services, families can get control over their worldwide assets, better plan for transferring wealth to the next generation and leverage our philanthropic expertise.”\nRodney Allen has more than 40 years experience in advising international families, businesses and organizations. He advises on the complex international business, estate, tax and philanthropic issues they face. His current clients include international families, their service providers and multi-national philanthropic organizations. He is also on the Boards of MSM and its subsidiary, as well as global trust companies.\nRodney’s experience began with a 9-year career at Arthur Andersen, where he specialized in cross-border tax issues for international companies and individuals. Next, Mr. Allen spent 10 years at Citibank, where amongst other assignments, was responsible for its International Wealth Structuring business and its EMEA Discretionary Asset Management sales department. He also served as General Manager of Citibank (Switzerland). After a short assignment as head of Credit Suisse’s Guernsey fund administration business, Rodney was appointed head of Barclays global trust business. In 2010, he took a 1-year leave of absence to return to university for an advanced law degree in Environmental Law, focusing on international environmental, human rights and other social-responsibility issues.\nRodney is a member of the Texas Bar and has passed the California CPA exam. He was awarded a JD from the University of Richmond in 1985 and an LLM from Oregon University in 2011. His undergraduate degree in English was awarded by James Madison University in 1979. Rodney currently resides in Switzerland, where he has lived and worked for the past 30+ years. He has also lived and worked in the United States and in The Netherlands.\nColin Woolcock\nBoard Member\n“Successful investing requires one to get not too greedy nor too fearful. It requires patience, discipline and controlling one’s emotions. Using Sailing as an analogy - It is how you set your sails and not the direction of the wind that determines which way you go.\nWe share over 100 years of financial markets experience and are passionate and committed in helping families navigate their wealth in all types of economic environments.”\nColin Woolcock has over 40 years of financial markets experience in senior positions working at Citibank in the Corporate and Investment Bank and Wealth Management across three continents (Argentina, Venezuela, Spain, Brazil, Indonesia, and Switzerland). His last position in Switzerland was Division Executive for Europe, Middle East, and Africa, for the Citi’s Wealth Management business.\nIn 2005, Colin moved to Deutsche Bank managing the Latin American and Southern European business in Geneva. In 2011, Colin successfully founded a real estate company Geneva Homes, which focuses on high value properties for Swiss and international clientele.\nColin Woolcock was educated at the British Schools in Montevideo, Uruguay, and at St. George’s College in Buenos Aires, Argentina. He has a degree in Business Administration from the Universidad Católica Argentina.\nColin is a Trustee on the Board of Governors of St. George’s College in Buenos Aires and was on the Finance Committee of the Jakarta International School. He was also a member on the Capital Contribution Committee to build the Nations Campus of the École International de Genève, and the Fund-Raising Committee for the new Arts Centre.\nColin Woolcock and his family have lived in Geneva for the past 25 years and he currently advises family offices alongside managing his real estate business.\nJohn Bottomley\nNon-executive Director\n“Real Estate investing can provide tax efficient diversification for wealthy families and institutions across a wide spectrum of risk profiles, property types and geographies.”\nJohn Bottomley has over 40 years of Global Real Estate expertise and is a recognized senior real estate executive.\nHe is a proven investor, lender, business development professional who has had positions with leading firms Berkshire Residential Investments, Rockefeller Group, Citigroup Property Investors, Travelers Insurance, Citi Private Bank London, and Citibank Canada.\nHe has served on the Management, Investment and Credit Committees in all of these businesses and lived and worked in Canada, London, New York and Tokyo.\nJohn currently advises several investment managers and high net worth family offices on real estate investment and funding strategies.\nHe has a MA in Regional Economics and Urban Planning from the University of Waterloo, Ontario and a Honors BA from York University, Toronto. He also holds Series 7 and 63 US Securities Licenses.\nJohn resides in New York, USA.\nMilan S. Morjaria\nExecutive Director\n“Our families’ collective net worth are in excess of USD 5 billion and their wealth is spread across three continents. Generational wealth from first-generation entrepreneurs is a powerful force, but its global, multi-continental spread demands bespoke, privacy-first wealth management that is as agile and ambitious as its creators.”\nMilan S. Morjaria is the Founder of MSM Investment Advisors SA, with over 38 years of experience in global financial markets. Drawing on his extensive background, he founded MSM Multi Family Office in Geneva in March 2010, later expanding its operations to Dubai in August 2020. The firm specializes in managing the wealth, transitions, and legacies of affluent global families and their charitable foundations.\nFrom 1988 to 2010, Milan built a distinguished 22-year career at Citigroup. He progressed through diverse roles, from currency trader and private banker to his final position as a Managing Director in Geneva, where he focused on Ultra High Net Worth clients and family offices. During his tenure, he was a member of the European leadership team and was a three-time recipient of the prestigious Chairman’s Council European Award (2005-2007). He also served on the board and investment committee for the Citibank Swiss pension fund.\nMilan holds a bachelor’s degree in economics from the London School of Economics and Political Sciences and has completed executive programs at London Business School and Harvard Business School.\nA resident of Switzerland, he is deeply committed to philanthropy, supporting Swiss non-profit organizations focused on children’s education and healthcare in developing countries.\nHe travels extensively to the United Kingdom, the Middle East,