ty of Richmond in 1985 and an LLM from Oregon University in 2011. His undergraduate degree in English was awarded by James Madison University in 1979. Rodney currently resides in Switzerland, where he has lived and worked for the past 30+ years. He has also lived and worked in the United States and in The Netherlands.\nColin Woolcock\nBoard Member\n“Successful investing requires one to get not too greedy nor too fearful. It requires patience, discipline and controlling one’s emotions. Using Sailing as an analogy - It is how you set your sails and not the direction of the wind that determines which way you go.\nWe share over 100 years of financial markets experience and are passionate and committed in helping families navigate their wealth in all types of economic environments.”\nColin Woolcock has over 40 years of financial markets experience in senior positions working at Citibank in the Corporate and Investment Bank and Wealth Management across three continents (Argentina, Venezuela, Spain, Brazil, Indonesia, and Switzerland). His last position in Switzerland was Division Executive for Europe, Middle East, and Africa, for the Citi’s Wealth Management business.\nIn 2005, Colin moved to Deutsche Bank managing the Latin American and Southern European business in Geneva. In 2011, Colin successfully founded a real estate company Geneva Homes, which focuses on high value properties for Swiss and international clientele.\nColin Woolcock was educated at the British Schools in Montevideo, Uruguay, and at St. George’s College in Buenos Aires, Argentina. He has a degree in Business Administration from the Universidad Católica Argentina.\nColin is a Trustee on the Board of Governors of St. George’s College in Buenos Aires and was on the Finance Committee of the Jakarta International School. He was also a member on the Capital Contribution Committee to build the Nations Campus of the École International de Genève, and the Fund-Raising Committee for the new Arts Centre.\nColin Woolcock and his family have lived in Geneva for the past 25 years and he currently advises family offices alongside managing his real estate business.\nJohn Bottomley\nNon-executive Director\n“Real Estate investing can provide tax efficient diversification for wealthy families and institutions across a wide spectrum of risk profiles, property types and geographies.”\nJohn Bottomley has over 40 years of Global Real Estate expertise and is a recognized senior real estate executive.\nHe is a proven investor, lender, business development professional who has had positions with leading firms Berkshire Residential Investments, Rockefeller Group, Citigroup Property Investors, Travelers Insurance, Citi Private Bank London, and Citibank Canada.\nHe has served on the Management, Investment and Credit Committees in all of these businesses and lived and worked in Canada, London, New York and Tokyo.\nJohn currently advises several investment managers and high net worth family offices on real estate investment and funding strategies.\nHe has a MA in Regional Economics and Urban Planning from the University of Waterloo, Ontario and a Honors BA from York University, Toronto. He also holds Series 7 and 63 US Securities Licenses.\nJohn resides in New York, USA.\nMilica Tsima\nOffice Manager\nOver 12 years of experience in administration within international companies.\nShe is responsible for office operations, HR, executive support and payroll coordination, working closely with senior management to ensure efficient day-to-day operations.\nPreviously worked at Energin Trading SA (Switzerland) as Director, Office Manager & HR.\nBA in Banking and Finance.\nFluent in Serbian, Croatian, English and French.\nToni Apostoloski\nPortfolio Manager\n“At MSM, our portfolio management process combines asset allocation and high conviction investment themes to ensure investment objectives are aligned with our client's long-term goals, risk appetite, tax and personal circumstances. Our investment capabilities are focused exclusively on areas in which we believe we can provide significant value to meet the expectations of families with sophisticated needs.”\nToni Apostoloski joined MSM as an Investment Analyst in 2019. Prior to joining MSM, Toni worked at Banque Heritage specializing in quantitative and qualitative research on equity and third-party funds.\nToni currently is a Portfolio Manager and member of the investment committee at MSM. He is responsible for MSM Thematic funds and products.\nHe has over 12 years of investment experience in managing discretionary and advisory portfolios across multi asset classes.\nToni holds a Bachelor in Economics and a Master’s degree in Finance (Financial Engineering and Risk Management) from HEC Lausanne. He is fluent in English and French.\nMarkus Bettels\nAML and Risk Officer\nMarkus Bettels is a seasoned risk, compliance, and clientservice professional with more than twenty years of experience supporting private clients and financial institutions. Based in Switzerland, he serves as Risk & AML Officer at MSM Investment Advisors SA, where he oversees regulatory compliance, risk management, and the integrity of client relationships. Markus also leads the firm’s Relationship Support Team and manages key aspects of its IT infrastructure, ensuring secure, efficient, and wellgoverned operations.\nBefore joining MSM, Markus spent seven years at Citibank Switzerland working closely with private bankers to deliver highquality wealthmanagement services to international clients. His background combines technical expertise with a strong commitment to service, discretion, and longterm partnership.\nMarkus holds a Bachelor of Arts in Political Science and Communication from Denison University and completed his schooling in Switzerland, including the International Baccalaureate program. He brings a global perspective shaped in part by extensive travel and a lifelong interest in different cultures.\nMichelle Di Franco\nRelationship 